# hoko configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/opencode/hoko.env (machine-local, survives a git pull) or
# to hoko.env in this repo, and uncomment what you want to change. Every setting has a
# working default, so an empty file is a valid configuration.
#
# Precedence, lowest first:
#   hoko.env in this repo  →  ~/.config/opencode/hoko.env  →  the real environment
#
# So a one-off override works too:
#   HOKO_PLAN_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash
#
# The plugin exports every setting into each shell an agent runs, which is how the
# skills read them.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- models -----
# "provider/model-id" — run `opencode models` for the list. Leave a model unset and that
# agent uses whatever model the session is on.

# The planning agent: grills the request and writes the plan.
#HOKO_PLAN_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash

# The build agent: conducts a plan run — reads every diff, decides on the reviewer's
# findings, commits. Also what plain build-mode chat runs on. Left unset it follows the
# session's model, whatever that happened to be when you approved the plan.
#HOKO_BUILD_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash

# The executor subagent: implements one plan step at a time.
#HOKO_EXECUTOR_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash

# The reviewer subagent: reviews a step's diff against the plan.
#HOKO_REVIEWER_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash

# The QA subagent: the end-of-run full gate, and it fixes what it finds.
#HOKO_QA_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash

# The research subagent: reads documentation and reports with citations.
#HOKO_RESEARCH_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- journal ----
# Where each cycle's prompt, plan and closing report are filed, one directory per
# project. There is no default: leave this unset and nothing is journaled — the
# workflow itself is unaffected. Point it at a notes vault, a plain directory, wherever.
#HOKO_JOURNAL_PATH=~/notes/journal


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- plans ---
# Where plans are written, relative to the repository root. The plan agent may edit
# nothing else, so changing this moves the one path it can write. The top-level segment
# is what execute-plan adds to .gitignore when the repo does not already track it.
#HOKO_PLANS_DIR=.ai/plans


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- gates ---
# The coverage floor the full quality gate holds to, as a percentage. A floor, not a
# target — the gate treats lowering it as a regression.
#HOKO_COVERAGE_MIN=85


# --------------------------------------------------------------- git flow ----
# Commit without asking for confirmation on the message (1 = on). The protected-branch
# check and the quality gate still apply, and pushing is never part of committing.
#HOKO_COMMIT_AUTO=1

# The branch that plays the `develop` role: what feature and bugfix branches are cut from
# and open their pull request against. Unset means `develop` when the repository has one
# and the remote's default branch when it does not, so a develop-flow repository needs
# nothing here. It never overrides a hotfix or release branch, which are cut from and
# target the release branch.
#HOKO_BASE_BRANCH=develop

# Push the branch and open the pull request without asking (1 = on). Left unset, the end
# of a run shows the base, branch and title and waits for confirmation. Only applies when
# origin is GitHub; any other remote leaves the branch for manual integration.
#HOKO_PR_AUTO=1


# ------------------------------------------------------- not read from here ---
# These two are opencode's own, read from the real environment at startup — the plugin
# cannot set them for you. Export them from your shell profile if you have leftover
# Claude Code files: opencode loads ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md as instructions and
# ~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md as skills, and an old copy of this workflow there will
# tell the model plans live in .claude/plans/.
#
#   export OPENCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT=1
#   export OPENCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE_SKILLS=1
